      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DTfby0rE0AO/",
      "caption": "The Three Body Problem is a classic problem in physics and mathematics that studies how three objects move under their mutual gravitational attraction. When only two bodies are involved their motion can be predicted exactly using simple equations. But when a third body is added the system becomes extremely complex.\nSmall changes in position or speed can lead to completely different outcomes which makes long term prediction very difficult. Because of this complexity there is no single general formula that solves the Three Body Problem in all cases. Only a few special solutions exist under perfectly idealized conditions such as specific symmetrical arrangements.\n\nThis problem is important in understanding planetary motion star systems and chaos theory\n\n#ThreeBodyProblem #PhysicsConcepts #Astrophysics #ChaosTheory #ScienceExplained\n[Three Body Problem , Gravitational interaction , Chaotic motion , Orbital dynamics , Idealized solutions]"
