      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CklPQ8JO9cS/",
      "caption": "Getting to the Federal Reserve\u2019s inflation target of 2% could require a painful recession. \u2060\n\u2060\nAlthough America\u2019s central bank must treat the target as sacred, the practice has surprisingly flimsy foundations\u2014and could yet be changed.\u2060\n\u2060\nKeeping inflation at 2% was first adopted in New Zealand in the early 1990s. Having decided to target inflation, policymakers had to pick some number. Gradually, the framework was aped by central banks around the world.\u2060\n\u2060\nThe Fed has been formally shooting for 2% inflation since 2012. But to read why some economists argue that the target should be higher, click on the link in our bio.\u2060\n\u2060\nIllustration: @kaltoons1"
