      "caption": "BREAKING: Claude can now run the same audit Marcus Aurelius ran on himself every day as Emperor of the World (for free).\n\nAurelius ruled the most powerful empire in history. He commanded armies, managed crises, and made decisions that shaped civilisation \u2014 alone at the top with nobody to answer to.\n\nEvery night he opened his private journal and ran the same audit on himself. Not his empire. Himself. The gap between who he was that day and who the moment demanded he become.\n\nHe did this for 19 years. We call it the Meditations. The most honest self-examination ever written.\n\nClaude now runs that exact audit on you.\n\nHere is the prompt. Four slides. One system. Run it before you plan anything else this week.\n\n(Save this. You will need it more than once.)"
