      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DWl3idbDEmr/",
      "caption": "In the Marvel universe, Tony Stark is often portrayed as having effectively unlimited AI resources, with systems like J.A.R.V.I.S., F.R.I.D.A.Y., and E.D.I.T.H. running across his suits, labs, and satellites. These AI systems handle everything from real\u2011time battle calculations to global surveillance, giving Stark the ability to deploy near\u2011instantaneous intelligence for any task without conventional constraints like processing power or access limits.\n\nWhile fictional, Stark\u2019s access illustrates the idea of AI-as-an-infinite utility, where agents can coordinate autonomously, predict outcomes, and execute highly complex tasks simultaneously. This exaggerates real-world discussions about AI capabilities, highlighting both the allure and potential danger of AI systems with few practical limits, a cautionary tale as companies push toward agentic AI platforms in reality. \n\nWould unlimited AI tokens change how humans work and create?\n\nFollow @ai.rise.co\n\n#fyp #life #ai"
