      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cs1nZ8fP1mD/",
      "caption": "Adult: \u201cHow was your day?\u201d \nChild: \u201cFine.\u201d\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nAdult: \u201cWhat did you learn today?\u201d\nChild: \u201cNothing.\u201d\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nAdult: \u201cWho are your friends?\u201d\nChild: \u201cNo one.\u201d\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nEver had an exchange like this with a kid? \n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nSame. There\u2019s a reason for this. These questions are too big and honestly too boring to get kids talking. \n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nInstead, try asking a S.O.C.K. question. S.O.C.K. questions are:\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\n\u2728 Specific\n\u2728 Open-ended\n\u2728 Creative\n\u2728 Kid-friendly\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nThe acronym might sound silly, but it is a quick and easy way to screen the questions you are asking the little ones in your life to make sure they are actually engaging and answerable.\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nLooking for more questions like this? Visit the link in my bio for a list of 225 S.O.C.K. questions on topics including:\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\n1. Icebreakers\n2. Getting Acquainted\n3. Wellness Checks\n4. Exploring Values\n5. Community Building\n6. Taking Responsibility\n7. Curriculum Connections\n8. Hopes & Dreams\n9. Discussion & Debate\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\nThis resource was designed for parents, teachers, counselors, and anyone else who works with children and can be used during one-on-one conversation, morning meetings, talking circles, journaling, and more. Comment TALK for the link \ud83d\udc97\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\n\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\n #kindergartenteacher #iteachk #iteach1st #elementaryteacher #primaryteacher #gentleparenting #gentleparent #momsofig #mindfulmama #lifewithlittles #igteachers #teachersofig #teachersfollowteachers #teacherlife #teacherproblems #ukteachers #aussieteachers #teachersdownunder #canadianteacher #parentsofteens #teachingresources #classroomideas #parentsofinstagram #teachertips #teacherinspiration #iteach5th #iteach6th #iteach #iloveteaching #iteachtoo"
