      "caption": "Sums Of 100 Using 9 Digits In Ascending Order\n\nA Computer was asked:  to use only the Digits/Numbers from 1 to 9, once only,  in ASCENDING Order, to make Sums of 100.\nIn seconds, it revealed the following 11 cases  of Consecutive Order or Natural Counting Order:\n\n123 - 45 - 67 + 89 = 100\n\n123 + 4 - 5 +67 - 89 = 100\n\n123 + 45 - 67 + 8 - 9 = 100\n\n123 - 4 - 5 - 6 - 7 + 8 - 9 = 100\n\n12 - 3 - 4 +5 - 6 + 7 + 89 = 100\n\n12 + 3 + 4 + 5 - 6 - 7 + 89 = 100\n\n1 + 23 - 4 + 5 + 6 + 78 - 9 = 100\n\n1 + 2 + 34 - 5 + 67 - 8 + 9 = 100\n\n12 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 67 + 8 + 9 = 100\n\n1 + 23 - 4 + 56 + 7 + 8 + 9 = 100\n\n1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6 + 78 + 9 = 100\n\n \n\n(Original Source of this Puzzle, from The Magic  Numbers Of Dr Matrix aka Martin Gardner)."
